## Mushroom paths

These are important folders in the structure that are all tagged with "#Mushroom".

Per-PC mushrooms (example):

| key            | value         |
| -------------- | ------------- |
| [[Root]]       | [[Root]]/     |
| [[Anju]]       | [[Anju]]/     |
| [[Anju color]] | #[[3ed7e4ff]] |
| [[Ash]]        | [[Ash]]/      |

/Anju/

## Centered Mushroom

Root/

## Mushroom paths

These are important folders in the structure that are all tagged with "#Mushroom".

Per-PC mushrooms (example):

_/Anju/
_/Ash/
_/Puy/
_/Rio/
_/Sora/
_/Tapioca/
\_/PCs/

## Mushroom colours

You can optionally declare per-mushroom colour mappings here. Each mapping is a simple
line of the form:

```
<path>=#rrggbb
```

Notes:

- Use the same path ids that the visualiser uses (directory ids end with '/').
- There is an automatic colour assignment (visualiser may override).
- Example entries:

```
Anju/ = #3ed7e4ff
Ash/  = #1d2088ff
Anju/ = #3e9f51ff   # alternate shorter path form
```
